          "say": "Water at 1.85 debye and ammonia at 1.47 are polar too.",
          "write": "H₂O 1.85 D, NH₃ 1.47 D"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Name the shape, not the domain geometry. Ammonia is trigonal pyramidal.",
          "write": "✗ NH₃ tetrahedral shape"
        },
        {
          "say": "Never put lone pairs axial in five-domain molecules.",
          "write": "✗ axial lone pairs"
        },
        {
          "say": "In AX four E two, the lone pairs go opposite. Not side by side.",
          "write": "✗ AX₄E₂ see-saw"
        },
        {
          "say": "Count lone pairs on the central atom, especially for xenon and halogens.",
          "write": "count central lone pairs"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Lewis structure, domains, A X E label, geometry, then shape.",
          "write": "Lewis → AXₘEₙ → shape"
        },
        {
          "say": "Lone pairs are bossy. They shrink bond angles.",
          "write": "109.5° → 107° → 104.5°"
        },
        {
          "say": "Five domains, lone pairs at the waist. Six domains, lone pairs opposite.",
          "write": "eq for 5,  trans for 6"
        },
        {
          "say": "Polar bonds plus a shape that doesn't cancel makes a polar molecule.",
          "write": "polar bonds + no cancel"
        }
      ]
    }
